A convex polygon has interior angles below 180 degrees, which corresponds to all cross products between consecutive edges being positive or all negative; zero means a straight angle, and a sign change means a reflex vertex. I take the first cross product and then scan the next two vertices of each triple, skipping the pair involving itself.

